@* Minimal "back to chart" affordance for full-page instruments
   (SailSteer / WindRose / Dashboard). Sits top-left of the page;
   a single tap routes to /. Purpose: a helm who drilled into a
   full-page instrument shouldn't need a round trip through the
   side nav to get situational awareness back.

   The chip renders as an <a> (not a <button>) so it respects the
   browser's own back-button semantics when middle-clicked /
   opened in a new tab. *@

<a class="plotter-back-chip" href="/" aria-label="Back to chart">
    <span class="plotter-back-chip-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#x2190;</span>
    <span class="plotter-back-chip-label">Chart</span>
</a>
